  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MunicipalRecord
  interactionName: Equipment Dispatch Sheet
  isInformationSource: 0
  npcProfile: 0
  openingLine: It's been a quiet day around here.
  choice1: Ask about Daniel
  response1: Daniel Mercer disappeared seven years ago.
  choice2: Ask about the town
  response2: Nothing much changes around here.
  informationID: anonymous_package
  informationTitle: Anonymous package
  informationSource: Anonymous package
  informationDescription: An anonymous sender sent me two waterworks records and a note claiming the original search missed something.
  informationType: 2
  isSceneExit: 0
  destinationScene: Diner_Investigation
  destinationSpawnID: 
  requiredInformationID: bell_job_ledger
  unavailableMessage: The dispatch sheets are organized by job reference. I should identify Bell's internal job entry first.
  department: GRAYFORD MUNICIPAL RECORDS
  documentTitle: Equipment Dispatch Sheet
  reference: WW-91-184
  documentDate: 09 OCT 1991
  documentBody: 'BELL MUNICIPAL SERVICES

    EQUIPMENT DISPATCH SHEET



    Date: October 9, 1991

    Job Reference: WW-91-184

    Destination: North County Waterworks



    Vehicle Assigned:

    Utility Truck 02



    Equipment:

    Portable drainage pump

    Inspection lamps

    General maintenance tools



    Crew:

    Two field personnel



    Dispatch Authorized By:

    F. Bell



    Return Time: Not entered

    Site Work Completed: Not indicated



    This sheet records an equipment assignment, not confirmation of work performed.'
  evidenceID: bell_dispatch_sheet
  evidenceTitle: Equipment Dispatch Sheet
  journalNote: A Bell Municipal Services dispatch sheet dated October 9, 1991, assigns Utility Truck 02, drainage equipment, and two workers to the North County Waterworks. No return time or completion status is recorded.
  evidenceSource: Bell Municipal Services
