  interactionName: Contractor Billing Copy
  isInformationSource: 0
  npcProfile: 0
  openingLine: It's been a quiet day around here.
  choice1: Ask about Daniel
  response1: Daniel Mercer disappeared seven years ago.
  choice2: Ask about the town
  response2: Nothing much changes around here.
  informationID: anonymous_package
  informationTitle: Anonymous package
  informationSource: Anonymous package
  informationDescription: An anonymous sender sent me two waterworks records and a note claiming the original search missed something.
  informationType: 2
  isSceneExit: 0
  destinationScene: Diner_Investigation
  destinationSpawnID: 
  requiredInformationID: municipal_status_ledger
  unavailableMessage: The billing files are organized by client and work order. I should establish the relevant municipal reference first.
  department: GRAYFORD MUNICIPAL RECORDS
  documentTitle: Contractor Billing Copy
  reference: WW-91-184
  documentDate: 15 OCT 1991
  documentBody: "BELL MUNICIPAL SERVICES\r\nCONTRACTOR BILLING COPY\r\n\r\nInvoice Reference: BMS-91-184\r\nRelated Work Order: WW-91-184\r\nDate: October 15, 1991\r\nBilled To: Grayford Public Works\r\n\r\nDescription:\r\nWaterworks lower-access inspection and associated service work.\r\n\r\nCharges:\r\nInspection and assessment \u2014 $180.00\r\nLabor allocation \u2014 $320.00\r\nEquipment use \u2014 $150.00\r\n\r\nTOTAL SUBMITTED: $650.00\r\n\r\nPayment Status: Not indicated on this copy.\r\n\r\nSupporting completion report: Not attached."
  evidenceID: bell_billing_copy
  evidenceTitle: Contractor Billing Copy
  journalNote: Bell Municipal Services submitted a $650 invoice for work associated with WW-91-184 on October 15, 1991. The available billing copy does not include a completion report.
  evidenceSource: Bell Municipal Services
